  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}.$ Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253135/assets/a6aeb42a84ab0d8ffbb7ef6898dd6cc45cb95c2fcb33aab0c6985455bd68db09.png)\n\nWe see that the function is not defined for $x<0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
